s it; you're constantly trying to figure out who you can trust. Meanwhile, aggression-based matchmaking allows you to play (mostly) your own way - with or against others. Agression-based matchmaking is much more reliable in solos, whereas in duos and trios the game is much more PvP-focused. The devs can be slow to add meaningful updates and patch issues, with a 6 monthly 'major' content roadmap. Hopefully the new map and content in October will freshen things up a bit.", "timestamp_created": 1782858713, "timestamp_updated": 1782858713, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1761816609", "hardware": {"system_ram": "65375", "os": "Windows 11", "cpu_name": "12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12600KF", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060", "vram_size": 7957}, "reactions": []}]}